#
# Conformance case: teleology/weak-vs-strong-plan.
#
# A weak plan vs a strong plan over the SAME two-branch nondeterministic outcome set: the strong plan reaches the goal on EVERY outcome (StrongPlanSuccess); the weak plan has one outcome that misses the goal and is NOT recoverable (WeakPlanSuccess).
#
# CRITICAL: the teleology evaluator seeds ONLY from input.nq world facts; this
# input.logic.ttl carries the minimal, clean-compiling, certifiable program axiom
# the projections need (no asserted teleology triples here — the world facts live in
# input.nq, exactly as the foundation conformance cases keep theirs).

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/teleology/weak-vs-strong-plan/> .

ex:GoalExpression a logic:GoalExpression .
